# Use this file to list any data files you want to download
# from S3. See github.com/NVDLI/s3_data_loader for more advanced
# options.
#
# Downloads land in the `course_data` volume, mounted at /dli/task/data in the
# lab, dind, course-prep and assessment containers (same absolute path
# everywhere, so a `docker run -v` source a notebook hands to the inner daemon
# resolves). VSS itself reads videos from its disposable data-dir inside dind;
# the course keeps the S3 copy here and ingests from it over the API of the
# VSS agent service.
#
# Add course files HERE. Do not place them into the volume by hand: a
# hand-placed file is lost the moment the volume is recreated.
#
# EVERY LINE IS A LAUNCH PRECONDITION. The loader is one sequential process.
# A key that does not exist, or a --recursive prefix with no objects
# (list_objects returns no 'Contents' key and the loader raises KeyError),
# stops it with a non-zero exit, and load-course-data.py writes FAILED with the
# error to /dli/task/data/.course-data-status.json. Compose no longer gates on
# the loader, so `up -d` and JupyterLab are unaffected, but vss-deploy and
# course-prep wait on that marker: they exit 1 with "S3 course data loader
# failed: ...", the VSS stack never comes up, and the onboarding notebook
# (sections 0.3 and 0.4) reports FAILED.
# Upload first, verify with `aws s3 ls s3://dli-lms/data/<prefix>/`, then list.
#
# HOW KEYS MAP TO /dli/task/data (loader behaviour verified on the devbox,
# Sep 3 and Sep 8 2026, by reading /dli/app/loader.py out of the image):
#   --recursive s3://dli-lms/data/<prefix>/   strips <prefix>/ and writes the
#                                             remainder of each key under /data,
#                                             folders preserved.
#   s3://dli-lms/data/<prefix>/a/b.mp4        the stock loader writes /data/b.mp4
#                                             (basename only). load-course-data.py
#                                             wraps the loader so that explicit
#                                             keys under the course prefix keep
#                                             their folder: /data/a/b.mp4. The
#                                             recursive course line then skips
#                                             them ("already exists locally").
# Do NOT add per-folder --recursive lines (s3://.../search-videos/): a recursive
# line strips what it lists, so that form flattens the folder into /data.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. The loader downloads sequentially in FILE order, and within a
# --recursive line in S3 list order (byte order). Small, needed-early items go
# at the TOP: the five clips below are what notebook 2 opens first
# (traffic_short.mp4) and what course-prep ingests for notebook 4 (the four
# search clips); the model caches (~80 GB) go last.
#
# THE LOADER LISTS AT MOST 1000 KEYS PER --recursive LINE. nvdli/s3_data_loader
# makes a single unpaginated list_objects call (its loader.py says so: "This
# returns a max of 1000 keys"). Everything that sorts after key #1000 under a
# prefix is silently never copied. Keep every recursive prefix under 1000 keys;
# anything that must land regardless of sort order gets its own line on its own
# sub-prefix. The prefixes below are: media + ground truth (tens of keys), the
# built docs site (88 keys, published 2026-11-05), the pinned
# model caches (83 keys, each verified against deploy/*-checkpoint.json by
# load-course-data.py).
#
# Course media. Filenames are the CONTRACTS.md section 7 names. The four
# search clips must match lab/task/search-videos.json (course-prep's manifest).
# The Part 1 assessment cuts its own clip from rain_eval.mp4. In VSS Coding
# Agent Skills the coding agent uploads its own copies of the four clips and
# loops normal_eval.mp4 through NVStreamer as a live stream.
s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2/traffic_short.mp4
s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2/search-videos/normal_eval.mp4
s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2/search-videos/rain_eval.mp4
s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2/search-videos/fog_eval.mp4
s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2/search-videos/night_eval.mp4

# Course documentation (the built Sphinx site, served in the JupyterLab UI by
# jupyter-server-proxy, see lab/configs/jupyter_configs/jupyter_server_config.py).
# Its own prefix, so it neither consumes the course listing's 1000-key budget
# nor perturbs byte order within it. The loader strips the listed prefix, so
#   c-fx-17-v2-docs/course-docs/...  ->  /dli/task/data/course-docs/...
# which is the DOCS_ROOT the Jupyter config serves. Build and trim as
# docs/course/README.md steps 1 and 2 say (never upload .doctrees/), then publish with:
#   aws s3 cp --recursive --acl public-read docs/_build/html/ \
#     s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2-docs/course-docs/
# and verify the listing is non-empty before a launch (see the precondition
# note at the top of this file).
#
# THE PART 1 LAUNCH NEEDS THE SITE TOO (2026-11-04). The site source is docs/
# (build and publish: docs/course/README.md). VSS Coding Agent Skills, the last
# step of Part 1, is a page of this site (docs/course/vss-coding-agent-skills.md),
# and the lab context file the coding agent reads is in it too
# (docs/_static/vss-lab-context.txt, which lands at
# /dli/task/data/course-docs/_static/vss-lab-context.txt). Without this line
# the Course Docs tile serves an empty directory, and that step cannot run.
# The prefix also holds the Part 2 pages (the Part 2 launch loads it from
# task2/data_sources), so the Part 1 launch shows them as well.
# ENABLED 2026-11-05: the site built from commit 2ccbb15 is uploaded, and
# `aws s3 ls --recursive s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2-docs/ | wc -l` printed 88.
# Never empty this prefix while the line is active: an empty --recursive
# prefix stops the loader and therefore the whole launch.
--recursive s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2-docs/

# The rest of the course prefix: ground_truth/ (search_videos.json, the
# labelled events that the Part 1 assessment checks against) and anything
# added later. The five clips above already exist
# locally by now and are skipped.
# load-course-data.py also skips a legacy rt-vlm-cache/ folder if one was copied
# across from the Berlin prefix.
# This line also downloads whatever else still sits under the prefix: the
# retired warehouse clips (warehouse/) and ground_truth/warehouse.json land on
# every VM until someone removes them from S3. Nothing in the course reads them.
--recursive s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2/

# Pinned model caches. Only the manifest-pinned rt-vlm/, nemotron/, rt-embed/
# and rt-cv/ versioned files are downloaded; load-course-data.py raises if any
# pinned file is missing from the listing. /data/models is the vss_models
# volume, so no extraction or second copy is needed; vss-deploy verifies sizes
# and checksums before selecting a directory.
--recursive s3://dli-lms/data/c-fx-17-v2-models/

# Keep this trailing blank line: the loader has been observed to ignore the last
